{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Vectors of the set reader (docs/dbspec.md \"Document sets\"). Each case is a file tree under an empty temporary directory, the root of the tree: a path maps to {\"file\": UTF-8 text}, {\"hex\": bytes}, {\"symlink\": target as written} or {\"hardlink\": the tree path of an earlier file}; parent directories are created. The runner calls the set reader with the tree root joined with `set`. A `want` with `documents` and `external` lists the joined paths, relative to the tree root, in order; the runner requires each returned path to be the tree root, `/`, and that path, and the bytes to equal the file's. A `want` with `errors` lists each error's rule and path in order, the path relative to the tree root; messages are not compared. Unknown or missing fields are errors.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "minimal",
      "tree": {
        "app/shop.dbs": {
          "file": "dbspec 1 shop\n"
        },
        "app/dbspec-set.json": {
          "file": "{\"schema\": 1, \"documents\": [\"shop.dbs\"]}"
        }
      },
      "set": "app/dbspec-set.json",
      "want": {
        "documents": [
          "app/shop.dbs"
        ],
        "external": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nested-and-external",
      "tree": {
        "app/shop.dbs": {
          "file": "dbspec 1 shop\n"
        },
        "app/billing/invoices.dbs": {
          "file": "dbspec 1 invoices\n"
        },
        "core/core.dbs": {
          "file": "dbspec 1 core\n"
        },
        "app/dbspec-set.json": {
          "file": "{\"schema\": 1, \"documents\": [\"shop.dbs\", \"billing/invoices.dbs\"], \"external\": [\"../core/core.dbs\"]}"
        }
      },
      "set": "app/dbspec-set.json",
      "want": {
        "documents": [
          "app/shop.dbs",
          "app/billing/invoices.dbs"
        ],
        "external": [
          "app/../core/core.dbs"
        ]
      }
    },
